{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ about $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038679/state.json" "file_sha256" "e1cb18b6c0a74882849e67940a8cdf21762f0af56e9de942ec5a8aee4d8e5681"} {"question" "q-8174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\n{P}_{4}(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3}+\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(a)}{4!}(x-a)^{4}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $a=1,$ so\n\n$$\n{P}_{4}(x)=f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2!}{(x-1)}^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(1)}{3!}{(x-1)}^{3}+\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(1)}{4!}{(x-1)}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSo we need to work out $f(1),$ ${f}^{′}(1),$ ${f}^{″}(1),$ ${f}^{‴}(1)$ and ${f}^{(4)}(1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & ⟹ &  & f(1) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡1=0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{x}={x}^{-1} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(1) & ={1}^{-1}=1 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-{x}^{-2} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(1) & =-(1)^{-2}=-1 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-(-2){x}^{-3}=2{x}^{-3} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(1) & =2(1)^{-3}=2 \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(x) & =2(-3){x}^{-4}=-6{x}^{-4} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{(4)}(1) & =-6(1)^{-4}=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${P}_{4}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x) & =0+(x-1)-\\frac{1}{2!}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{2}{3!}(x-1)^{3}-\\frac{6}{4!}(x-1)^{4} \\\\  & =(x-1)-\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(x-1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(x-1)^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038679/state.json" "file_sha256" "e1cb18b6c0a74882849e67940a8cdf21762f0af56e9de942ec5a8aee4d8e5681"} {"question" "q-8174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Cour